# Store every text file with LF in the repository — Git's canonical form.
# Windows checkouts still get CRLF in the working tree (core.autocrlf), so
# nothing changes for editors, but a file edited on Windows no longer flips
# its entire contents in the diff.
#
# Before this, the index was split 44 CRLF / 41 LF: whoever touched a file
# decided its endings, and a four-line change showed up as a 306-line diff
# (v0.9.3 reported 3098 changed lines where only 241 were real).
#
# Applied once with `git add --renormalize .` — that commit is listed in
# .git-blame-ignore-revs so `git blame` skips over it.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) a checkout rewrites them to CRLF, the shebang becomes `bash\r`,
# and the script dies on WSL/Linux with:
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# That silently disabled ./precommit_check.sh on every Windows clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
